WEBVTT

00:11.460 --> 00:14.480
<i>The scent's fading.</i>

02:02.110 --> 02:04.590
This girl, too, I think.

02:04.590 --> 02:06.980
The same as Simeon, huh?

02:07.890 --> 02:11.660
<i>The Testament of Carnamagos</i> 
is sapping her magic power.

02:12.980 --> 02:15.100
<i>The Testament of Carnamagos</i>?

02:16.210 --> 02:17.560
Erm...

02:17.560 --> 02:20.930
It's a book on sorcery that 
can fatally harm people.

02:21.540 --> 02:23.810
It's deemed forbidden.

02:24.380 --> 02:25.620
Forbidden...

02:26.200 --> 02:27.370
At this rate,

02:27.370 --> 02:31.130
it's just going to keep sucking her power away,
no matter how much we supply her.

02:31.840 --> 02:33.750
That's a problem.

02:38.690 --> 02:43.280
Maybe I can trace where her 
magic power is being taken.

03:00.320 --> 03:01.600
Or not.

03:01.600 --> 03:02.500
See?

03:03.440 --> 03:08.360
I can't tell if that's the nature of the spell, 
or if they're concealing themselves...

03:08.770 --> 03:12.670
We'd have to catch the attacker in the act.

03:13.470 --> 03:16.420
It's a nasty spell. That's for sure.

03:16.950 --> 03:21.280
I suppose it was thanks to Chise 
that Lucy was awake until just now.

03:21.280 --> 03:22.370
Probably.

03:22.800 --> 03:27.040
I suppose it would take a Sleigh Beggy 
to provide more than what's being taken.

03:27.650 --> 03:30.990
But if they intended to sap her to death...

03:30.990 --> 03:32.040
No!

03:32.750 --> 03:38.220
Neither of them have so much magic power 
that they'd be worth stealing from, either.

03:38.630 --> 03:39.950
Exactly.

03:39.950 --> 03:42.740
We don't know why they were 
chosen to be victims.

03:44.080 --> 03:47.240
Either way, it's a problem 
for me that it's these two.

03:47.240 --> 03:48.120
Huh?

03:48.120 --> 03:52.360
Chise's going to do something 
reckless again for Lucy.

03:53.000 --> 03:55.980
And Simeon might become my friend.

03:57.270 --> 03:59.700
It's a pain, but I need to 
get to the bottom of this.

03:59.700 --> 04:00.850
Oh, wow.

04:00.850 --> 04:01.910
I'm surprised.

04:01.910 --> 04:06.990
<i>Lindel-san and Rahab-san were only 
"acquaintances," and now Elias has a friend?</i>

04:07.620 --> 04:08.930
I'll...

04:08.930 --> 04:11.380
I'll do anything I can to help.

04:11.380 --> 04:13.930
I can't have you putting yourself in danger.

04:14.320 --> 04:18.450
Besides, this incident is not one 
for children to be involved in.

04:18.690 --> 04:20.880
It doesn't involve you, either, Elias.

04:20.880 --> 04:24.200
But still, you said you would act 
for Simeon-sensei's sake.

04:24.200 --> 04:27.750
I'm acting partly for your sake, as well.

04:27.750 --> 04:30.080
Then it <i>does</i> involve me.

04:30.080 --> 04:33.240
She's my class—my friend.

04:33.790 --> 04:39.130
I still don't understand that part of you.

04:39.130 --> 04:40.120
Hey!

04:40.120 --> 04:42.010
You're a child. Stay out of this.

04:42.450 --> 04:45.200
Don't you see that he's worried for you?

04:47.350 --> 04:51.050
Anyway, I'm going to go 
report to the principal.

04:51.050 --> 04:54.490
Don't mention this to anyone, all right?

04:55.180 --> 04:56.810
There's an extra class today.

04:56.810 --> 04:58.890
It might help take your mind off things.

05:14.080 --> 05:15.510
Philomela.

05:17.570 --> 05:18.800
Morning.

05:19.490 --> 05:20.590
Morning.

05:22.480 --> 05:23.580
Um...

05:24.550 --> 05:26.650
The potpourri you gave me...

05:27.620 --> 05:29.600
It's starting to fade.

05:30.860 --> 05:32.040
So...

05:40.770 --> 05:43.280
<i>The fabric's all worn out.</i>

05:44.510 --> 05:46.540
Do you want a new pouch?

05:46.540 --> 05:48.290
Or should I change it out?

05:49.190 --> 05:50.290
Change it out...

05:50.610 --> 05:52.360
with the same scents.

05:57.410 --> 05:58.680
<i>I smell blood.</i>

05:59.550 --> 06:01.920
Want to make some together sometime?

06:04.150 --> 06:06.580
Is that something I could do?

06:06.580 --> 06:09.340
I'll bring more kinds.

06:15.840 --> 06:18.340
Someday, then.

06:18.880 --> 06:21.420
Okay. Someday.

06:23.520 --> 06:27.810
Today's extra lesson is on rune sorcery.

06:28.200 --> 06:33.830
Runes were originally used in everyday 
life as a phonetic writing system.

06:33.830 --> 06:39.090
To use them in sorcery takes a degree 
of knowledge and familiarity.

06:39.690 --> 06:43.890
Each character is said 
to have its own meaning.

06:43.890 --> 06:45.420
In addition to divination,

06:45.420 --> 06:49.090
they're also used for all kinds of protective
 amulets, as well as offensive sorcery.

06:49.440 --> 06:53.550
You can expect them to be quite versatile.

06:54.140 --> 06:55.960
The meanings of each...

06:54.960 --> 06:57.320
<i>This looks like a thorn.</i>

06:58.050 --> 07:00.120
Are you curious about that rune?

07:00.120 --> 07:01.380
Yes.

07:01.730 --> 07:04.320
That rune is called Thurisaz.

07:04.320 --> 07:08.880
Giants, faeries, and Thor, 
the god of lightning...

07:09.450 --> 07:11.150
And thorns.

07:11.150 --> 07:12.320
Brambles.

07:12.820 --> 07:14.180
Thorns.

07:14.750 --> 07:18.710
You could use it for protection, 
but I wouldn't recommend it.

07:18.710 --> 07:24.300
It won't necessarily protect you in 
the way a human would prefer.

07:27.030 --> 07:28.050
All right.

07:28.050 --> 07:32.510
Today, we'll practice using runes 
to make a protective amulet.

07:32.510 --> 07:33.770
Okay.

07:33.770 --> 07:36.020
Which one should I use?

07:36.020 --> 07:37.390
I think...

07:36.530 --> 07:37.550
Chise.

07:37.390 --> 07:38.620
I like this one!

07:38.300 --> 07:40.600
How's Lucy been?

07:38.620 --> 07:39.700
Looks nice!

07:39.700 --> 07:41.090
It's pretty.

07:41.090 --> 07:42.000
It suits you.

07:42.000 --> 07:42.860
Really?

07:42.860 --> 07:44.860
How about this one?

07:56.150 --> 07:57.380
Zoe.

07:58.290 --> 07:59.280
Did I wake you?

07:59.750 --> 08:02.410
Chise told me you collapsed again.

08:02.410 --> 08:04.040
You should keep resting.

08:04.540 --> 08:06.160
What time is it?

08:06.160 --> 08:07.440
It's night.

08:07.440 --> 08:10.370
I got Alexandra's permission.

08:11.130 --> 08:12.410
My brother...

08:12.410 --> 08:13.050
Huh?

08:13.480 --> 08:15.000
You have a brother?

08:15.770 --> 08:17.270
Never mind.

08:17.820 --> 08:18.930
Err...

08:18.930 --> 08:20.350
Yeah, you should get more sleep.

08:20.820 --> 08:21.670
Yeah.

08:22.360 --> 08:23.830
Um...

08:23.830 --> 08:26.690
Anyway, I just wanted to say hi.

08:27.270 --> 08:28.270
Your snakes...

08:28.270 --> 08:28.900
Huh?

08:29.620 --> 08:33.490
Can I pet your snakes?

08:34.150 --> 08:34.990
Huh?!

08:36.860 --> 08:38.770
What? Is there a problem?

08:38.770 --> 08:41.890
No, I mean...

08:52.950 --> 08:55.480
I used to have spiders.

08:58.620 --> 09:01.330
I adored them so much.

09:02.590 --> 09:03.850
Yeah?

09:04.800 --> 09:06.540
Hey, Lucy...

09:06.860 --> 09:13.150
You shouldn't be so quick to ask other 
Gorgons to let you touch their snakes.

09:13.720 --> 09:17.140
That has a special meaning for us...

09:22.670 --> 09:24.320
Oh, well.

09:26.890 --> 09:28.760
<i>Ah, youth.</i>

09:32.730 --> 09:36.360
We're going to be living 
at school for a while.

09:38.320 --> 09:42.160
Lucy's a little better when I'm around.

09:42.160 --> 09:44.630
I want to do what I can for her.

09:44.630 --> 09:46.470
I have a dorm room, too.

09:48.470 --> 09:49.660
I'm sorry.

09:49.660 --> 09:51.960
I'll come back if you ever need me.

09:51.960 --> 09:54.140
It's only until we solve this problem.

09:55.750 --> 09:57.160
Elias?

09:57.160 --> 09:59.350
Elias had to stay back.

09:59.890 --> 10:02.830
He says grown-ups have responsibilities.

10:04.030 --> 10:05.680
Hey, Silver...

10:07.040 --> 10:11.230
<i>Our</i> Elias says he's doing it for his friend.

10:11.230 --> 10:12.510
Isn't that amazing?

10:12.950 --> 10:17.670
I'm happy, yet I'm conflicted, and...

10:18.500 --> 10:20.460
I don't know how to describe it...

10:30.790 --> 10:33.670
Okay, I'm going outside for a bit.

10:35.420 --> 10:36.830
Don't worry.

10:36.830 --> 10:38.720
I won't be far.

10:47.590 --> 10:48.910
I brought it.

10:55.670 --> 10:56.860
Contract...

10:56.860 --> 10:58.360
As per our contract...

10:58.360 --> 10:59.320
Meat.

10:59.320 --> 11:00.250
Good.

11:00.250 --> 11:01.210
Good.

11:01.210 --> 11:02.630
Good.

11:04.850 --> 11:08.480
Man, I can't believe you thought to do that.

11:08.740 --> 11:12.990
Thank you for preparing the sheep.

11:13.300 --> 11:14.610
And for accompanying me.

11:14.850 --> 11:19.610
I got the payment, and I had access.

11:20.050 --> 11:22.580
Where did those sheep come from?

11:22.580 --> 11:28.440
Sacrificial animals are usually 
sheep, goats, or chickens.

11:28.870 --> 11:33.090
There are plenty of guys around 
who work with that kind of thing.

11:33.440 --> 11:35.120
I see.

11:39.360 --> 11:41.590
You seem down.

11:41.590 --> 11:44.930
They were raised as for that to begin with.

11:44.930 --> 11:46.340
Don't sweat it.

11:47.870 --> 11:49.380
I'm sorry.

11:49.730 --> 11:54.110
I'm just bothered by the fact that 
I couldn't repay them myself.

11:56.820 --> 12:00.540
You're pretty straight-laced. 
Or rather, you're quite an idiot.

12:02.100 --> 12:05.020
Who goes out of their way to 
defend someone they don't know,

12:05.020 --> 12:07.540
especially when that person 
was after their life?

12:07.960 --> 12:12.200
You don't think ahead, do you?
 You just expect things to work out.

12:12.850 --> 12:15.110
I can't argue against that.

12:16.610 --> 12:18.930
Your man's got it rough.

12:20.350 --> 12:23.380
What would you have done if 
they hadn't settled for sheep?

12:23.890 --> 12:26.540
Would you have snatched 
someone off the street?

12:26.540 --> 12:29.510
Or would you have been fine 
with being eaten yourself?

12:30.690 --> 12:32.130
Well...

12:32.130 --> 12:35.530
That's the kind of creature 
you're dealing with.

12:36.110 --> 12:41.530
There are tons of people who broke their promise
 and were killed or ended up going mad.

12:41.530 --> 12:45.710
The whole damn world's 
unfair enough as it is.

12:45.710 --> 12:49.110
What's the point in taking bad bets?

12:53.530 --> 12:57.200
I'm sure I want to live.

12:58.080 --> 13:02.060
But I keep acting before I realize it.

13:03.650 --> 13:08.040
How can I learn to think about 
myself when I do things?

13:08.470 --> 13:09.430
Patience.

13:10.760 --> 13:12.180
Patience...

13:12.180 --> 13:14.230
Observe carefully.

13:14.230 --> 13:15.740
Don't jump.

13:15.740 --> 13:18.870
Even pack wolves each have their role.

13:18.870 --> 13:21.940
Watch to see who should be doing what.

13:22.470 --> 13:27.300
But when I'm in a position 
to act first, I...

13:27.300 --> 13:28.620
Listen.

13:29.070 --> 13:32.840
Is it really other people that 
you're so eager to protect?

13:32.840 --> 13:36.070
Or are you just being greedy 
and trying to be important?

13:37.310 --> 13:39.120
Me? Greedy?

13:39.410 --> 13:43.780
If you want to save everyone 
in sight, that's up to you.

13:44.400 --> 13:46.080
But keep in mind that if you get hurt,

13:46.080 --> 13:49.690
there's someone who's going to feel 
that pain just as much as you.

13:50.050 --> 13:54.400
Besides, you aren't the only one
 they might take their share from.

13:54.400 --> 13:56.830
And I mean both the hounds
 and the world at large.

13:57.570 --> 14:00.590
What if you aren't enough for them?

14:01.010 --> 14:02.720
What if they take your friends?

14:02.720 --> 14:03.360
I won't...

14:03.360 --> 14:06.900
You know what you need to do to 
make sure that doesn't happen.

14:07.550 --> 14:10.780
I'm neither your friend nor your parent.

14:10.780 --> 14:12.570
I won't tell you what to do.

14:13.690 --> 14:15.880
I'll keep it in mind.

14:21.840 --> 14:23.730
The sun's coming up.

14:25.360 --> 14:27.540
Trick-or-treat!

14:27.540 --> 14:29.830
Stop it, dummy! I'm getting wet!

14:29.830 --> 14:33.460
Treats or not, I'm still trolling you!

14:33.460 --> 14:35.520
Trick-or-treat!

14:35.520 --> 14:36.910
Here's your treats.

14:37.540 --> 14:39.320
Thank you.

14:40.140 --> 14:42.750
This is all the decorations we have, huh?

14:42.750 --> 14:44.180
What a shame.

14:44.180 --> 14:46.490
I guess the treats are the important part.

14:46.490 --> 14:47.570
Honestly, though...

14:47.900 --> 14:51.430
To think I'd be handing 
out treats with <i>you</i>...

14:51.790 --> 14:53.030
What can you expect?

14:53.860 --> 14:56.540
The instructors are far too busy right now.

14:57.240 --> 14:59.150
The theft of that book...

14:59.570 --> 15:01.090
The attacks...

15:01.720 --> 15:05.550
And the possibility that the 
perpetrator is in the College.

15:05.880 --> 15:08.660
I know things are hectic.

15:08.660 --> 15:13.100
But at the same time, it'd be 
suspicious if we canceled an event.

15:13.970 --> 15:18.630
My guess is that it was 
one of the undergrounders.

15:19.020 --> 15:21.230
Undergrounders? You mean the waste tower?

15:21.450 --> 15:23.800
I guess that would make the most sense.

15:24.220 --> 15:27.940
Why are you handing out 
candies if you know so much?

15:27.940 --> 15:32.280
To be honest, I'm not particularly 
interested in this incident.

15:32.280 --> 15:37.410
So I should at least let the kids 
enjoy the event, shouldn't I?

15:37.410 --> 15:39.040
Uh-huh.

15:39.510 --> 15:41.740
Well, I'm off, now.

15:42.370 --> 15:43.460
Tristan.

15:45.890 --> 15:48.310
I told you not to call me by that name.

15:48.810 --> 15:49.890
I'll smack you.

15:50.980 --> 15:52.330
I'm just messing with you.

15:53.540 --> 15:54.730
Jeez.

16:00.500 --> 16:01.800
Take this!

16:05.000 --> 16:06.670
<i>Right, today's Hallowe'en.</i>

16:06.670 --> 16:07.400
Ack!

16:10.730 --> 16:12.040
Come on!

16:14.190 --> 16:15.780
Watch where you're going!

16:15.780 --> 16:17.320
Wait, she's older than us.

16:17.710 --> 16:19.640
S-Sorry.

16:24.020 --> 16:25.170
You there...

16:25.170 --> 16:25.970
Yes?!

16:26.580 --> 16:29.600
Could you lend me that 
when you're done with it?

16:31.740 --> 16:33.590
Let go of me!

16:33.590 --> 16:35.070
I won't!

16:36.350 --> 16:38.100
Um...

16:38.100 --> 16:41.170
Get off me, already!

16:41.170 --> 16:43.460
You might collapse again!

16:43.460 --> 16:45.080
Go back to bed!

16:45.080 --> 16:46.890
What's going on here?

16:47.230 --> 16:49.690
I have work on Hallowe'en!

16:50.660 --> 16:54.290
It's not somewhere you should be when 
you know you're going to collapse!

16:54.500 --> 16:57.600
That's why I'm going <i>before</i> I collapse!

16:57.600 --> 16:59.900
Don't let go of her, Chise.

16:57.910 --> 17:00.740
<b>Grrrrrip</b>

16:59.900 --> 17:00.740
Yup.

17:01.260 --> 17:06.000
<i>Is this what people feel like when they
 stop me or get mad at me for being reckless?</i>

17:06.380 --> 17:08.040
Let me go!

17:08.480 --> 17:10.590
I need money for tuition!

17:10.990 --> 17:13.840
Isn't Seth-san paying for you?

17:14.930 --> 17:17.350
I don't want to touch that money.

17:17.810 --> 17:20.570
He'll just use it as 
an excuse to boss me around.

17:21.860 --> 17:24.190
Either way, you can't be out and about now.

17:24.190 --> 17:25.520
Go back to bed.

17:25.520 --> 17:26.670
No!

17:27.470 --> 17:29.400
What are you fussing about?

17:29.400 --> 17:31.410
We came to see how you're doing, but...

17:32.250 --> 17:34.280
Chise, you're hurting me.

17:34.280 --> 17:35.440
Oh, sorry...

17:35.850 --> 17:38.910
Lucy insists on going to the waste tower.

17:38.910 --> 17:40.790
The waste tower?

17:40.790 --> 17:42.430
What's that, again?

17:42.430 --> 17:45.420
It's one of the towers that 
makes up the College.

17:45.420 --> 17:47.910
Students don't get to go there often.

17:48.620 --> 17:51.600
Rumor has it that's 
where they keep the results

17:51.600 --> 17:55.290
of botched sorcery and other 
stuff they can't get rid of.

17:55.820 --> 17:59.450
You can also find rare ores
 and medicinal herbs.

17:59.450 --> 18:02.470
It's true that you can get 
paid to collect them...

18:02.470 --> 18:04.550
I didn't think you'd be 
working <i>there</i>, though.

18:05.280 --> 18:08.090
I'm sure that's shocking to 
a good little boy like you.

18:08.570 --> 18:11.810
Anyway, I've already signed 
up to do it again this year.

18:12.470 --> 18:14.570
I'm going to have an 
instructor with me there.

18:14.570 --> 18:15.210
I'll be fine—

18:15.210 --> 18:15.900
No!

18:15.900 --> 18:18.380
If you really need to go...

18:15.900 --> 18:18.380
I don't know what you need, but...

18:18.380 --> 18:20.810
...I'll go instead.

18:21.500 --> 18:22.340
Huh?

18:35.580 --> 18:36.920
Hey!

18:37.980 --> 18:39.450
Not home.

18:41.140 --> 18:42.270
Oh, well.

18:42.270 --> 18:44.390
We can inform them later.

18:44.390 --> 18:46.180
Let's get going.

18:46.180 --> 18:46.920
Okay.

18:47.680 --> 18:50.180
I really appreciate you coming along.

18:50.890 --> 18:54.800
There are fewer and fewer 
qualified students each year.

18:56.300 --> 18:57.620
Hello.

18:58.520 --> 19:01.210
Is this the entrance to the waste tower?

19:02.440 --> 19:03.590
Philomela.

19:04.120 --> 19:05.070
Chise.

19:05.730 --> 19:06.950
And...

19:07.820 --> 19:09.180
So...

19:09.180 --> 19:12.870
Lucy Webster was supposed to be 
here for the gathering practical.

19:12.870 --> 19:17.490
She couldn't make it, so 
we came in her place.

19:17.490 --> 19:18.850
Practical...

19:19.800 --> 19:21.200
I see.

19:21.200 --> 19:22.320
I'm sure she's grateful.

19:23.400 --> 19:25.970
Has Webster told you what you're collecting?

19:25.970 --> 19:26.780
No.

19:27.260 --> 19:29.270
I'll explain along the way, then.

19:30.700 --> 19:32.280
I'm Fabio.

19:32.650 --> 19:34.220
Fabio Zaccheroni.

19:34.880 --> 19:35.970
Thanks for the help.

19:42.340 --> 19:45.310
Don't look so upset.

19:45.310 --> 19:47.190
I don't like guarding you, either.

19:47.500 --> 19:50.070
You should have gone with Chise, then.

19:50.320 --> 19:53.740
She told me to keep an eye on 
you so you don't sneak out.

20:00.260 --> 20:03.330
Please don't do anything 
reckless the way Chise does.

20:04.090 --> 20:09.920
I don't have bowels anymore, but your 
brother's got a stomach that can ache.

20:10.320 --> 20:12.350
It's not reckless.

20:12.940 --> 20:14.130
I'm...

20:14.130 --> 20:15.080
Lucy.

20:15.740 --> 20:17.390
Ms. Wachmann.

20:17.390 --> 20:19.440
I heard you were ill.

20:19.900 --> 20:21.430
Are you feeling all right?

20:21.430 --> 20:23.680
Yes. I'm sorry.

20:23.680 --> 20:26.050
I know I applied to participate 
in the gathering practice...

20:26.930 --> 20:28.670
It's dangerous there.

20:28.670 --> 20:31.620
I'll find you another gathering 
task once you're feeling better.

20:32.560 --> 20:35.030
I can handle this one myself.

20:36.380 --> 20:38.870
Have you run into my classmates?

20:44.700 --> 20:46.730
Are you working, too, Philomela?

20:47.210 --> 20:48.840
I'm just helping.

20:48.840 --> 20:49.680
Always?

20:50.580 --> 20:51.920
Sometimes.

20:52.630 --> 20:53.450
Chise...

20:54.210 --> 20:56.100
Watch out for that man.

20:57.490 --> 20:59.270
Now, students...

20:59.950 --> 21:01.350
Brace yourselves.

21:01.950 --> 21:05.070
Plants and animals that went 
extinct and were once lost.

21:05.510 --> 21:09.200
Precious minerals that make the heart skip.

21:09.940 --> 21:13.250
Those who were discarded, yet 
are not even allowed to wither,

21:13.860 --> 21:16.780
and even those whose hearts were stolen...

21:17.220 --> 21:20.210
This place can be overwhelming, 
so be careful.

21:32.550 --> 21:34.590
Hello, Mother.

21:35.800 --> 21:39.230
I'm dealing with one problem after another.

21:39.670 --> 21:42.050
Now, what shall I do?

21:42.540 --> 21:44.690
Where should I begin?

21:45.910 --> 21:49.800
Ah, it's not that I'm not having fun.

21:49.800 --> 21:52.710
The more problems, the better.

21:53.050 --> 21:55.430
That's my job, after all.

21:55.920 --> 21:58.580
And the more I can solve, 
the better my reputation.

22:01.880 --> 22:03.710
You're awful.

22:04.490 --> 22:08.690
I suppose I should start 
with all these letters.

22:09.060 --> 22:09.810
Hm?

22:19.970 --> 22:24.030
Philomela Sergeant is withdrawing 
from the College, I see.
